+ * __dispatchlqmChangedEvent of iOS 16.5 reads (at least 0xb4 bytes): a flag byte, then its value: RSSI 0/+4 (int32), SNR 0xb/+0xc
+ * (int16), noise 0xe/+0x10 (int16), CCA 0x12/+0x13 (byte); then 32-bit counters (+0x14.. TX fail, retrans, frames; +0x20 RX retry;
+ * +0x24 RX frames), rates +0x40 TX, +0x44 TX fallback, +0x48 RX. Flag bytes at +8, +0x30, +0x31, +0x50, +0x62 and +0xa0
+ * ask for more (per-core RSSI, beacons, QBSS, roam, CCA statistics): left 0 here.
